WEBVTT

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:09.150
Hooded seals live in the Arctic.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:14.780
Did you all know

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.990
that the hooded seal's lactation period is about four days?

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:21.450
They say that's the shortest of any mammal.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.120
But setting that aside...

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:27.670
Japan is currently in the height of spring.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:31.420
As a rain of pollen tickles my nasal membranes,

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:35.430
I, Andou Natsuki, have officially become a high school student.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:38.930
Today is club recruiting day.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.560
High school is amazing!
There are so many different clubs!

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.700
H... H... Help me up...

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:01.990
I guess spring also brings along
some things I don't understand.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.120
Stray seal!

00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:09.340
What was that all about?

00:01:09.790 --> 00:01:11.340
Hey, Nattsun!

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.130
Um... Who are you?

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.800
I'm Furuhashi! Furuhashi!

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:19.050
We went to middle school together!

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:20.430
This happens a lot!

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.350
Nattsun, your jokes are really too much.

00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:26.350
I thought I told you to stop calling me
that once we were in high school.

00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:29.060
Well? Have you picked your club yet, Nattsun?

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:31.610
Are you sticking with the Tennis Club?

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.530
Hmm... But doing the same thing as in middle school

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.070
wouldn't be very exciting.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.280
Maybe I should be bold and try the Hundred Poems Club!

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:43.120
Huh?

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.120
Look! It's even the same arm motion.

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:49.130
I don't know if it's wise to join a club based on that.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.210
I don't like dealing with the hierarchies in clubs, anyway.

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.380
Maybe I should join the Going Home Club.

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.140
Really? Natsuki, you're joining the Going Home Club, too?

00:01:59.890 --> 00:02:02.640
Um... you're Touno, right?

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.220
Yeah! I'm Touno Karin. It's nice to meet you!

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:07.350
But I'm so glad.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:10.060
I thought I would be the only one joining the Going Home Club.

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:13.020
No, I really doubt that...

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.860
Furuhashi, you could join the Going Home Club—

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.240
What?! No, I've got my Hundred Poems Club!

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.030
Wasn't that just some idea you had?

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:24.490
Oh, right. I should go there and observe, or something.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:25.490
That's right, that's right...

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.500
Observe?

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.580
Well, why don't we do the same?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.840
Observe the Going Home Club! Yeah, right.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.170
Sure, let's go!

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.260
Huh? What?

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:42.510
No, the Going Home Club isn't...

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:44.010
a...

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.260
real...

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:46.970
club...

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:52.020
It<i> is </i>real!

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.240
Wait a minute.

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:26.780
Why does the Going Home Club have its own club room?!

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.620
That's taking "anything goes" too far!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:30.740
It's amazing, isn't it?

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.160
Come in!

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:34.620
Have a little doubt here...

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.010
Excuse us!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:44.010
Your membership is approved!

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.380
That was fast!

00:04:45.380 --> 00:04:47.550
But you're applying for membership, right?

00:04:47.550 --> 00:04:48.470
Yes!

00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:50.310
I'm not really...

00:04:50.310 --> 00:04:54.270
I'm so happy. What might your names be?

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.650
I'm Touno Karin!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.520
I'm Andou Natsuki.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:00.520
Karin and Natsuki, then!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:05.200
Right! Let me introduce the crazy
members of the Going Home Club!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.160
What?! The members are crazy?!

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.950
Sixteenth heir to the ancient
Hagizuki-ryuu martial arts style

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.250
Oohagi Botan.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.210
Let's fight bears together!

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.330
What?! She's exceptional!

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:22.010
Daughter of the head of the Kokonoe Corporation
Daughter of the head of the Kokonoe Corporation

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:24.130
Kokonoe Claire!

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.050
If we get any more members, we'll have to hire a maid.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:30.350
What?! She's exceptional, too!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.930
And I am the Going Home Club's president,

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:36.310
proud bearer of type A blood,
born under the sign of Taurus...

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:39.650
Doumyouji Sakura!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:47.280
That means you're just an ordinary person!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.780
L-Look.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:53.660
I appreciate the introductions,

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.120
but I'm not actually interested in joining your club...

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:59.380
So can I go home now?

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:01.250
You...

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.260
You're incredible!

00:06:05.590 --> 00:06:08.260
You want to go home right away...

00:06:08.260 --> 00:06:11.760
You have incredible Going Home Spirit within you!

00:06:12.010 --> 00:06:12.720
Huh?

00:06:13.760 --> 00:06:14.720
That's right!

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:17.390
We must order dresses for the two of you right away!

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:18.520
Huh? W-Wait!

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:21.770
We've got some real Uber Loogies among us now.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.650
If you're talking about an impressive newcomer,

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.280
the term is "Super Rookie"!

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.030
We've got two spirited first-years joining us!

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:30.660
This should be a lot of fun!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.200
Welcome to the Going Home Club!

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:41.790
It's too soon for the ending theme!

00:06:48.550 --> 00:06:51.680
So you ended up joining the Going Home Club yesterday!

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.510
This is no laughing matter.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:55.430
But it's so funny, Nattsu—

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:57.930
Uh, I mean, um, Natsukichi?

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:01.900
You don't have to invent a new nickname for me, Furukawa.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.230
It's Furuhashi.

00:07:04.570 --> 00:07:08.650
Anyway, they told me to start coming officially, today.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.820
What am I gonna do?

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:15.830
Well, it looks like not going isn't an option.

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:24.540
Hey, Natsuki.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:28.590
You can call me Natsuki. And I'll call you Karin.

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.340
Really? Then can I call you Natsuki?

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.720
Sure, fine with me.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:36.560
So, what is it?

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:37.560
Natsuki.

00:07:40.850 --> 00:07:45.610
Natsuki...

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.360
Um...

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:51.070
Oh, that's right.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:54.320
Natsuki, what do you think they
do in the Going Home Club?

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:57.160
You don't know?!

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.790
That's what I wanted to ask!

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:01.710
And what made you want to join

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.420
if you don't even know what they do?

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:07.170
What? Well, it was during club recruiting day...

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:12.590
Stand! Stand up!

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.350
This is it!

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:19.470
<i>What</i> is it?!

00:08:19.470 --> 00:08:22.180
What about that made you want to join their club?!

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.560
And they were recruiting people with that?!

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.690
I want to go home already.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.610
That's a Super Rookie for you!

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:30.820
Shut up already.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:33.400
It's okay, Natsuki.

00:08:33.400 --> 00:08:35.410
If you ask our upperclassmen in Japanese,

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:38.830
I'm sure they'll tell you what the Going Home Club does.

00:08:38.830 --> 00:08:42.410
Well, yes, that's probably true...

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:47.170
But it didn't occur to me that I had
a language choice besides Japanese.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:49.670
Mohawk Seal!

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:52.840
Excuse me.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.170
The first-years are here!

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.260
Welcome!

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:57.890
I've got controllers ready for you.

00:08:57.890 --> 00:09:00.510
Oh, that's right. Chairs, chairs!

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.600
Um, Sakura...

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:05.850
Take no great pains. Prithee call me Sakura.

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:07.480
Okay, Sakura—

00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:09.110
Aye, come nearer.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:13.360
Sakura, why are you
using such old-timey language?

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:16.070
Probably because sixth period was classic literature.

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.610
She's so easily influenced!

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:20.450
Natsuki. You wanted to ask something else, remember?

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:21.700
Oh, yeah.

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:23.620
Sakura.

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:27.420
What exactly does the Going Home Club do?

00:09:35.420 --> 00:09:36.630
We have fun!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:40.050
I told you, it's too soon!

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.930
How desperate are you to end the show?!

00:09:42.970 --> 00:09:47.270
If you do nothing, your youth will pass by in an instant.

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.270
That is why we formed the Going Home Club,

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.900
to enjoy ourselves as much as possible

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.900
after school and on the way home.

00:09:54.610 --> 00:09:56.700
Is that what it was?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:58.740
Not even your own members knew?!

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:02.780
We want to do things that are fun, but that one shouldn't do.

00:10:02.780 --> 00:10:04.240
Do things it's okay to do!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.080
But today, we're going to do something it's okay to do.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.750
Botan! Claire!

00:10:10.710 --> 00:10:12.460
What are you going to do?

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:15.710
We're going to the park to feed the pigeons.

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:17.760
Feeding the pigeons!

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.380
Project Code...

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:20.760
MANNA!

00:10:20.760 --> 00:10:23.260
It doesn't need a title that cool!

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:33.270
Feeding the pigeons? What are they, little kids?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.280
There!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:50.250
It's so fun!

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:54.750
Yeah! He took it!

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:59.130
Come on, little guy! It's tasty!

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:06.640
I guess... it might be kind of fun.

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.470
Just open it normally!

00:11:49.980 --> 00:11:55.690
So, that was Botan's demonstration
of Hagizuki-ryuu martial arts!

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.690
I'm impressed that you can cut it

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:02.950
so cleanly with just your bare hand.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:05.950
To be precise, I'm not cutting it with my hand.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:07.950
By moving my hand very quickly,

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.450
I create a momentary vacuum in the air.

00:12:10.450 --> 00:12:12.710
That's what cuts it.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.790
It's the same principle as the kamaitachi.

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.710
There it is! A manga explanation!

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:20.960
It's a closely guarded family secret, so don't tell anyone.

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.550
What?! You're taking a closely guarded secret pretty lightly!

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:28.260
But Botan really is strong, isn't she?

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.930
Yes. She's had many heroic exploits, as well.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:34.850
Especially her "Bear Tour" last summer.

00:12:34.850 --> 00:12:36.980
That was really scary!

00:12:38.060 --> 00:12:41.490
What kind of ominous-sounding tour is that?

00:12:41.490 --> 00:12:45.240
Botan kept us up to date with very detailed emails...

00:12:45.950 --> 00:12:47.950
July 28th.

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:50.240
I'm fighting a brown bear in Hokkaido.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:51.450
I knew it!

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.960
Why would you do something like that?!

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:56.040
I heard that the brown bear was the strongest

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.380
wild animal in Japan.

00:12:57.380 --> 00:12:59.130
So I didn't have a choice.

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:00.050
Yes, you did!

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.960
And your reason doesn't have a shred
of high school girlishness in it!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.100
The match was decided swiftly.

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:10.930
Was that all?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:12.520
I was left with only disappointment.

00:13:12.520 --> 00:13:14.520
You beat it?!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.940
I beat the brown bear!

00:13:15.940 --> 00:13:18.100
But I'm bummed by how weak it was.

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.940
Its punches looked like they weren't even moving.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:20.770
Teehee.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.690
It's a little late to bring out the

00:13:22.690 --> 00:13:24.990
high school girl mannerisms in your emails!

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.400
And, send!

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:30.490
Don't get cocky... just because you beat me...

00:13:30.490 --> 00:13:35.000
In Alaska, there dwells a bear far more powerful than I...

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:38.250
I felt as if the downed bear was speaking to me.

00:13:38.250 --> 00:13:41.130
No! It absolutely was <i>not</i> speaking to you!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.260
So, the brown bear was defeated.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:52.970
But he was the weakest of us Four Bear Kings, so—

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.520
That didn't happen! I know it didn't!

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.850
July 30th, Alaska.

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:01.400
You flew to America?!

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:04.280
I found a grizzly in the forest.

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.320
Truly, he was a full size larger than the brown bear.

00:14:12.990 --> 00:14:15.250
"I'm in America right now!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.710
I'm shocked by how big American hamburgers are!

00:14:18.710 --> 00:14:20.540
I'm so stuffed!"

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:24.210
All you did was enjoy your first trip to America!

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.960
"And then I beat the bear."

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.010
The bear doesn't even matter anymore, does it?!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:32.220
After defeating the grizzly, I realized...

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:35.810
Now that I'd come this far, I had to take on a polar bear.

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:37.520
Why?!

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.980
Bears get bigger and stronger the further north you go.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.690
And I'd started feeling like I was playing a fighting game.

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:47.150
She's got game brain...

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.280
July 31st.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.910
I beat the polar bear, as well.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:55.790
You did it?!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.660
She beat the strongest bear

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.920
and we all assumed it was over.

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:02.670
But there was still more to come.

00:15:02.670 --> 00:15:04.750
About a month later...

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.840
I read my cell phone bill and fell to pieces.

00:15:09.340 --> 00:15:12.050
It's because you used your cell phone so much overseas!

00:15:12.760 --> 00:15:15.470
It seems it wasn't bears I should have been fighting.

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:17.020
It was the system!

00:15:18.350 --> 00:15:20.440
The system known as rate structure!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.850
Just fix your rate plan and your lifestyle!

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:27.030
There were lots of others besides the bears.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.780
She beat a great white shark in the ocean near Japan,

00:15:30.780 --> 00:15:33.200
beat an elephant in Africa,

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.410
played with a squirrel at Tsurugaoka Hachiman Shrine,

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.370
beat a cobra in India...

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.750
I think a Kamakura vacation memory got

00:15:40.750 --> 00:15:42.460
mixed up in there somewhere.

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.340
She also beat the Demon King with just the

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:48.170
Hero and no orbs of light!

00:15:48.170 --> 00:15:51.630
And she beat the hardest final boss without taking any damage.

00:15:51.630 --> 00:15:53.640
There's just no end to her heroic exploits.

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:56.720
Those last two were just challenge run stories!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.770
That's how you end up with game brain!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.930
The point that I want to instill

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:03.270
in you first-years as club president is that

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:07.570
Botan can only do these things because she received special training.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.280
Ordinary people shouldn't try to mimic her!

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.440
Okay.

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.410
I've never heard a more unnecessary warning in my life.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:15.450
That's right!

00:16:15.450 --> 00:16:17.660
Now that we have new club members,

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.750
why don't you come fight bears with me for real?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:25.540
We're going to that new crepe stand today.

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.460
Let it go.

00:16:30.800 --> 00:16:35.340
Umm... I was sure it was in this area...

00:16:35.340 --> 00:16:37.430
Oh, is that it there?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:44.560
A bear!

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:45.810
Stop it.

00:16:50.320 --> 00:16:52.070
Sorry for the wait!

00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:56.610
Sakura, your crepe is so big!

00:16:56.610 --> 00:16:58.370
Can you really finish all that?

00:16:59.530 --> 00:17:01.200
Eh? Where's Natsuki?

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.870
I believe she went to the powder room.

00:17:27.020 --> 00:17:29.230
What's wrong? That was a strange noise.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:32.360
The truth is...

00:17:32.650 --> 00:17:36.150
at lunch, I went to the school store with Natsuki...

00:17:37.110 --> 00:17:39.660
But they were sold out of erasers.

00:17:40.120 --> 00:17:43.240
The school store can sell out of erasers?

00:17:43.240 --> 00:17:44.500
Yes...

00:17:44.500 --> 00:17:46.620
Well, they actually did have some.

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.920
A whole display of them.

00:17:47.920 --> 00:17:48.630
Huh?

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:53.130
But Karin didn't want one unless it was in a pink case.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:57.380
I couldn't erase at all during my afternoon classes.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.050
Just compromise and buy one!

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.300
That's tough.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:06.100
Let's go buy you a stationery store later.

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:09.850
Buy a store?!

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:16.780
Well, it can't be helped.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.700
Claire is the daughter of the Kokonoe Corporation, after all.

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:23.240
Her money sense is a little
different from a normal person's.

00:18:23.240 --> 00:18:25.200
That's more than "a little" different!

00:18:25.200 --> 00:18:26.910
Buying a store at the drop of a hat

00:18:26.910 --> 00:18:29.710
is like "real-life sugoroku with actual
trains" level of money sense!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:31.080
I just bought the whole store!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.090
Claire doesn't feel any sense of loss

00:18:34.090 --> 00:18:35.550
when she spends money.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.920
What are you talking about?

00:18:38.760 --> 00:18:42.300
You know how when we turn on the faucet,

00:18:42.300 --> 00:18:44.100
as much water comes out as we want?

00:18:44.100 --> 00:18:45.310
Yeah...

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:48.060
That's how money is for her.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:51.190
So she literally goes through money like water?

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:54.690
Her speech and behavior have always been extravagant.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.440
She can summon a helicopter with the slightest gesture.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.110
Or reserve an entire family restaurant.

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.500
My. Is that so?

00:19:10.460 --> 00:19:13.080
Why did you get so many frames just now?!

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:15.300
What? I wasn't even thinking about it.

00:19:15.300 --> 00:19:17.420
Try to avoid excessive movement!

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:20.180
This show is limited to *** frames!

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.720
This is what you call a true rich girl.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.350
President, you saw right through it!

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.270
What? Everything's gone white...

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.520
I guess the effects are showing.

00:19:29.520 --> 00:19:31.310
The seal is white, too.

00:19:31.690 --> 00:19:33.610
These are the storyboards!

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:35.900
This is the linework!

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:41.570
But Claire's really living life on easy mode, huh?

00:19:41.570 --> 00:19:44.780
You've always been able to get whatever you wanted, right?

00:19:46.160 --> 00:19:49.580
Actually, it's more that by the
time I realize I want something,

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.790
I already have it.

00:19:51.790 --> 00:19:55.710
She's on full auto mode! This is just like a crap game!

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:58.000
Hey, Natsuki!

00:19:58.000 --> 00:20:00.340
Be careful about making statements that could be construed

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:01.840
as calling movie-heavy games crap!

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:03.930
I didn't say anything like that!

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:06.100
Why are you being so oversensitive?!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:07.720
Missile seal!

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:11.680
Setting that aside, you may be wondering why

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:14.440
such a rich girl would attend a school for normal people.

00:20:14.690 --> 00:20:17.400
It's because Claire has always longed for

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:18.900
a normal high school life.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.950
I don't know if that's possible in a club like this.

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:25.320
It was my dream to walk home from school and attend

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:27.160
balls with my friends like a normal person.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:29.290
In what dimension is that normal?

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:31.750
What? Was I wrong?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.580
Well, that's the shape of it.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.420
Natsuki, Karin.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.290
You're both masters when it comes to being commoners,

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:39.800
so show her the ropes.

00:20:39.800 --> 00:20:41.670
Okay! Just leave it to me!

00:20:42.010 --> 00:20:44.340
Claire, did you know about this?

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:46.590
The most delicious part of the ice cream

00:20:46.590 --> 00:20:48.260
is not the ice cream itself,

00:20:48.260 --> 00:20:50.220
but the part that gets stuck to the lid!

00:20:50.520 --> 00:20:52.140
Oh, really?

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:54.600
That's not a "commoner" thought, it's a child's thought!

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.520
Ice cream...

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:00.860
comes with lids?

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.860
Okay! Today...

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:06.450
We will buy ice cream from the convenience store!

00:22:37.540 --> 00:22:40.170
Ice cream in a cup really is the best.

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:41.880
This is the way to go.

00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:44.670
Buy ice cream in a cup!

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:47.590
Natsuki here!

00:22:47.590 --> 00:22:50.260
I heard giant anteaters give birth standing up.

00:22:50.680 --> 00:22:52.050
Spawning standing up?!
